WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.800
US forces will leave their final Iraq bases by Wednesday, ending a two-decade military presence in a country where 4,500 Americans died. This is Omni View, episode 190. American forces are scheduled to leave their last remaining bases in Iraq by Wednesday. The pullout follows an agreement reached in 2024 under President Joe Biden and carried out by the Trump administration. Iraqi security experts say the withdrawal removes a military presence

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.340
that has acted as a counterweight to Iranian influence for years.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.080
The move occurs even as Washington continues military action against Iran.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.220
Iran and its allies inside Iraq view the departure as a strategic victory

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.040
that could allow greater influence over security and political decisions.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:52.040
Jassim Al-Bahadli, an Iraqi security analyst specializing in armed Shiite groups,

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.660
stated that pro-Iranian militia groups will portray the exit as a victory

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:00.000
and seek to translate that momentum into greater control.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.280
Other observers note that the timeline was set years earlier through bilateral talks,

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.560
with the 2024 framework fixing the sequence of base closures and equipment transfers.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:16.500
Iraqi officials have described the process as the end of a foreign military footprint that

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.040
began after 2003.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.900
Those same officials warned that the vacuum could also allow groups such as Islamic State to

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:24.600
stage a comeback.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.260
back. The South China Morning Post frames the exit as the conclusion of long planned bilateral

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:36.420
steps rather than a sudden shift. Al Jazeera emphasizes how the withdrawal opened space for

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.440
Iranian-aligned actors to expand their role in Iraqi affairs. Even those who see strategic gains

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:48.800
for Iran acknowledge that the original 2024 pact still permits some limited training and intelligence

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.240
operations cooperation after combat units depart.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.040
What happens next?

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:58.700
The first base closures begin this week, and Iraqi security forces will assume full control

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.860
of the remaining sites.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.960
Malaysian authorities started sending nearly 1,500 Myanmar nationals held in immigration

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.660
facilities back to their home country on Tuesday.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:14.540
The operation forms part of a government-to-government agreement to return up to 5,000 people.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.320
Officials describe the returns as voluntary under a bilateral program.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:24.620
Human rights groups have warned that returnees could face persecution or forced conscription

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.740
in Myanmar's ongoing conflict.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:33.500
The program continues despite those warnings, with the first group of 1,476 people already

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.160
in transit.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:40.580
Kuala Lumpur has framed the effort as a managed, orderly process conducted under agreed bilateral

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.440
terms between the two governments.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:48.860
students. Student demonstrations over conditions in French high schools led to more than 160 arrests

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:55.100
and dozens of injuries. The unrest occurred ahead of a presidential election. Police reported

00:02:55.100 --> 00:03:00.600
clashes during several marches across the country. Senior politicians from different parties have

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.940
blamed one another for the escalation and the resulting violence. Organizers say the protests

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:11.200
highlight long-standing problems of overcrowding and poor facilities in secondary schools.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.780
The events have intensified political debate about education funding and infrastructure in the

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.820
run-up to the vote. President Javier Miele said Argentina would sue Britain over the sea-line

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:28.280
oil project near the disputed Falkland Islands. The islands are administered by the UK,

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:33.460
and developers Navitas and Rockhopper hold British-issued exploration licenses.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:41.400
The 1982 conflict between the two countries, which killed 255 British and 649 Argentine

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.680
troops, remains a reference point in official statements.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.440
Argentina maintains its claim to sovereignty over the territory and views the oil development

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.000
as a violation of its rights.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.720
Developers argue they hold valid licenses issued by the British government.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.540
The threat of arbitration adds another layer to the long-standing sovereignty dispute.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:08.960
Japanese motor maker Nidek expects to record an impairment loss exceeding 600 billion yen or about

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:16.180
$3.8 billion. The charge relates mainly to its electric vehicle traction motor systems. The company's

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:23.040
share price fell 17% after the report surfaced. Sources indicated the loss stems from underperformance in

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:29.540
the EV segment, where Nidek has faced ongoing challenges scaling operations. The impairment reflects

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.020
complex difficulties in turning the traction motor business into a profitable line, despite

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.120
earlier investments.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:42.100
Six Samsung Group companies will invest $1 billion in Helix digital infrastructure, a company

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.660
backed by global investment firm KKR.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.460
The move expands the conglomerates activities beyond semiconductor production into the physical

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.260
system supporting AI growth.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:58.340
Samsung has described the step as part of its response to rising demand for data center capacity.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:04.400
Heelix focuses on AI-ready facilities, and the investment marks a shift toward infrastructure

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.200
that powers the global AI boom.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.120
Progressworth knowing comes from Japan's Science Ministry, which plans to develop improved

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:17.040
induced pluripotent stem cells that are easier to use in clinics and cheaper to produce.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:21.120
The goal includes treatments for strokes and chronic kidney failure.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.840
Researchers at institutions such as Kyoto University are involved in the effort.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:32.760
Current IPS technology can replicate complex organs but faces hurdles in cost and clinical application.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:40.140
The Ministry aims to create cells that lower those barriers, building on earlier work that established the first generation type.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:44.940
The program seeks to make the cells more practical for widespread medical use.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:53.040
To really understand how troop withdrawal timelines are set and executed, begin with the bilateral agreements that lock in both the schedule

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.320
and the handover of facilities years before the final date.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:02.400
In the Iraq case, the 2024 framework set the sequence of base closures and equipment

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.880
transfers, giving each side predictable steps rather than an abrupt departure.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:12.340
Those agreements also include clauses on residual training missions or intelligence sharing

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.000
that can continue after combat units leave.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:20.620
The same structure appears in earlier U.S. drawdowns from other countries, where the calendar

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.220
was adjusted only after new security guarantees were negotiated.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.420
One concrete check is to look for the text of the original status of forces agreement,

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:33.840
and any later amendments that list the exact basis and dates involved.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:39.340
Another is to compare the original timeline with any public updates issued by the government's

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:39.840
involved.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:45.440
Readers can also examine whether equipment transfers or training programs are mentioned separately

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.140
from the Clombat Unit Exit.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:52.640
This approach reveals whether the withdrawal is truly complete or whether narrower forms

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.500
of cooperation persist under the same legal umbrella.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.340
If you want to go deeper on the U.S. withdrawal from Iraq, compare how the South China Morning

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:06.540
Post and Al Jazeera are covering the same sequence of base closures and regional implications.

